/A 1145 0 R
/Alt (Nine bar charts labeled A to I display various data points:A. Gender distribution: 450 females, 29 males, 21 missing.B. Weight categories: less than 50 kg \(6\), 50-70 kg \(110\), more than 70 kg \(14\), missing \(370\).C. Age groups: less than 18 \(4\), 18-65 \(208\), 26-65 \(89\), more than 65 \(3\), missing \(196\).D. Reporters: consumer \(22\), other professionals \(110\), physician \(317\), pharmacist \(50\), missing \(1\).E. Outcomes: disability \(7\), hospitalization \(121\), life-threatening \(31\), death \(108\), other serious events \(219\), missing \(14\).F. Reported countries: U.S. \(101\), France \(68\), Canada \(45\), Poland \(39\), Portugal \(34\), other countries \(213\).G. Reported years: 2020 \(11\), 2021 \(25\), 2022 \(60\), 2023 \(173\), 2024 \(154\), 2025 \(77\).H. Time to onset: 0-30 days \(123\), 31-60 days \(12\), 61-90 days \(7\), 91-120 days \(3\), 121-150 days \(1\), 151-180 days \(4\), 181-360 days \(7\), more than 360 days \(2\).I. Indications: breast cancer \(337\), lung cancer \(19\), bladder cancer \(13\), transitional cell carcinoma \(131\), other indications \(19\).)
/K [1 1146 0 R]
/P 104 0 R
