/A 1210 0 R
/Alt (Four Kaplan-Meier survival curves analyzing different factors with time to event in days. A: Gender comparison, showing females and males with respective median times of 13 and 10 days \(p = 0.024\). B: Age comparison, adult and elderly groups both with a median of 12 days \(p = 0.81\). C: Reporters' status, consumers vs. professionals, median times are 14 and 12 days \(p = 0.68\). D: Cancer type indications, with median times for bladder cancer \(8 days\), breast cancer \(12 days\), and lung cancer \(12 days\), with p = 0.0095.)
